    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178-a3">

                <pb facs="0444" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg360"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in Mr. Phelps’s No.
                    351.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Captain
                            McDonald.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bonne Bay</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 12,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: lam instructed to give you notice that the
                    presence of your vessel in this port is in violation of the articles of the
                    international convension of 1818 between Great Britain and the United States in
                    relation to fishery rights on the coast of Newfoundland, and of the laws in
                    force in this country for the enforcement of the articles <pb facs="0445"
                        n="361" xml:id="pg361"/> of the convention, and that the purchase of bait or
                    ice, or other transaction in connection with fishery operations, within 3 miles
                    of the coasts of this colony, will be in further violation of the terms of said
                    convention and laws.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>N. N. TAYLOR,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Officer of
                                Custom.</hi></item>
                            <item>Capt. <hi rendition="#small-caps">James McDonald</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Schooner Thomas F. Bayard.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
